E["quest:92914"] = {t="quest",n="Strange Pylons",z="shendralas",s="In Shen'dralas, a depleted crystal pylon leaves its purpose unknown. You are asked to look for others nearby.",h="In Shen'dralas, a depleted crystal pylon leaves its purpose unknown.",sec={{t="Among the Ruins",b="A strange crystal rests on an ancient pedestal among Shen'dralas's elven ruins. Mere moments ago, emaciated mana elementals guarded it. The gemstone is fractured and its magic is nearly spent, leaving its purpose a mystery. You search the area for other pylons like it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the strange pylon?",a="It is a fractured gemstone set on an ancient pedestal in Shen'dralas. Its depleted magic leaves its purpose unknown.",al={"strange pylon","crystal pylon","what is this crystal"}},{q="Why is the crystal humming?",a="A weak hum of power comes from the fractured gemstone, though its magic is heavily depleted.",al={"crystal hum","why is it humming","weak hum"}},{q="What was guarding the crystal?",a="Emaciated mana elementals guarded the crystal mere moments ago.",al={"mana elementals","what guarded it","elementals by the pylon"}},{q="Where are the other pylons?",a="You are asked to search Shen'dralas for other pylons like the one you found.",al={"other pylons","find more pylons","pylon locations"}}},kw={"crystal","elven ruins","gemstone","mana elementals","pylon","shen'dralas","strange pylons"},rel={"zone:shendralas"},m={id=92914},src={"In-game quest text: Strange Pylons"},fv=true}
E["quest:93016"] = {t="quest",n="A Brief History Lesson",z="shendralas",s="You are sent to Shen'dralas to hear about the crystals you repaired. Their lights have drawn concern, and an explanation is waiting.",h="You are sent to Shen'dralas to hear about the crystals you repaired.",sec={{t="Questions in Shen'dralas",b="The crystals you repaired have raised questions, and you are sent to Mordent Evenshade in Shen'dralas for answers. The skies have taken on a dramatic appearance, adding to the unease around the earlier requests.",sp=0},{t="A Visit Planned",b="Mordent says his silence came from excitement at seeing the crystals shine again. He hopes to visit the temple of Shen'dralas, though he lacks the courage to speak with the Shen'dralar there.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is supposed to explain the crystals?",a="Mordent Evenshade in Shen'dralas is asked to explain the crystals you repaired.",al={"who explains crystals","Mordent info","crystal explanation"}},{q="Why did the earlier requests seem suspicious?",a="The requests came without context, and the skies had taken on a dramatic appearance.",al={"why suspicious","what was strange","why no context"}},{q="Why did Mordent leave out the explanation?",a="Mordent says he was eager to see the crystals' lights shine again and failed to explain the situation from the start.",al={"why no explanation","Mordent reason","why did he wait"}},{q="Does Mordent plan to visit the temple?",a="Mordent is excited to visit the temple of Shen'dralas again, though he says it may take time before he can speak with the Shen'dralar there.",al={"temple visit","Mordent going there","Shen'dralas temple"}}},kw={"a brief history lesson","crystal lights","crystals","dramatic skies","mordent evenshade","shen'dralar","shen'dralas","temple"},rel={"zone:shendralas"},m={id=93016},src={"In-game quest text: A Brief History Lesson"},fv=true}
E["quest:93362"] = {t="quest",n="What They've Done to My Peonies",z="shendralas",s="Mithera mourns both her lost necklace and the corruption that has gripped the Forlorn Garden. She asks you to grant a swift and merciful end to the tormented flora suffering in Shen'dralas.",h="Mithera mourns both her lost necklace and the corruption that has gripped the Forlorn Garden.",sec={{t="Mercy in the Overgrowth",b="Grief weighs heavily on Mithera as she lingers within Shen'dralas. Her precious necklace is missing, yet the agony of her beloved garden pains her even more deeply. The flora in the Forlorn Garden has turned wild and angry from whatever twisted power touched the soil. Knowing the suffering plants can feel pain, she seeks someone to thin their ranks swiftly before further harm befalls them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the garden to be culled?",a="Mithera gives the request from Shen'dralas, grieving over her lost necklace and her suffering plants.",al={"who gives what they've done to my peonies","peonies quest giver","who is mithera"}},{q="Where is the Forlorn Garden located?",a="The Forlorn Garden lies near Shen'dralas, where the local plant life has grown twisted and hostile.",al={"forlorn garden location","where are the peonies","where to cull plants"}},{q="Why does Mithera want the plants culled?",a="The plants have grown enraged and twisted from suffering. Mithera wants them granted a swift and merciful end because they can feel pain.",al={"why kill the plants","why cull the flora","peonies quest reason"}},{q="What else has Mithera lost?",a="Mithera lost her necklace, though she considers the chances of recovering it unlikely.",al={"mithera lost item","what happened to mithera necklace","mithera necklace"}}},kw={"flora","forlorn garden","mithera","necklace","peonies","shen'dralas"},rel={"zone:shendralas"},m={id=93362},src={"In-game quest text: What They've Done to My Peonies"},fv=true}
E["quest:93394"] = {t="quest",n="Meeting the Magister",z="shendralas",s="A Shen'dralar contact asks you to find Magister Kirandis inside the temple of Shen'dralas. The meeting concerns the temple's restored pylons and your place among its wary denizens.",h="A Shen'dralar contact asks you to find Magister Kirandis inside the temple of Shen'dralas.",sec={{t="At the Temple",b="The grand structure draws your attention, and a Shen'dralar contact points you toward Magister Kirandis. The magister is an old friend of the one who sent you and may welcome your presence. The Shen'dralar may be wary, so you are asked to approach them with respect.",sp=0},{t="The Pylons",b="After you find Kirandis, the magister sees that the pylons' power shines again. Their return binds the Shen'dralar fully to Shen'dralas. Kirandis urges you to meet the temple's denizens, whose wariness may ease with time.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who am I supposed to find?",a="You are asked to locate Magister Kirandis inside the temple of Shen'dralas.",al={"find kirandis","magister meeting","kirandis temple"}},{q="Where is Magister Kirandis?",a="Magister Kirandis is inside the temple of Shen'dralas.",al={"kirandis location","where magister","temple kirandis"}},{q="Who is Kirandis to the person who sent me?",a="Kirandis is an old friend of the Shen'dralar contact who sent you.",al={"kirandis friend","old friend magister"}},{q="Will the Shen'dralar welcome me?",a="The Shen'dralar may be wary of your presence, but you are asked to tread respectfully.",al={"shen'dralar wary","will they like me","shen dralar welcome"}},{q="What has happened to the pylons?",a="Their power shines again, and Kirandis says this binds the Shen'dralar fully to Shen'dralas.",al={"pylon power","temple pylons","pylons restored"}},{q="What should I do after meeting Kirandis?",a="Kirandis encourages you to meet some of the temple's denizens, who may be wary at first.",al={"meet denizens","what next kirandis","shen'dralas people"}}},kw={"kirandis","magister kirandis","meeting the magister","pylons","shen'dralar","shen'dralas","temple"},rel={"zone:shendralas"},m={id=93394},src={"In-game quest text: Meeting the Magister"},fv=true}
E["quest:93404"] = {t="quest",n="Rot and Regret",z="shendralas",s="Woodwyrd, the ghost of an ancient treant at the Forlorn Gardens, asks you to put out the flame that still burns him. He points you toward sacred water in Maraudon.",h="Woodwyrd, the ghost of an ancient treant at the Forlorn Gardens, asks you to put out the flame that still...",sec={{t="A Spirit's Burden",b="The ancient spirit says its final mistake binds it to this place, where it still feels a flame in death. It asks you to seek pristine water from a sacred ravine across Mashan’she. Maraudon is the place named, and the spirit is Woodwyrd himself, who awaits the Vial of Earth Song Water at the Forlorn Gardens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the water?",a="Woodwyrd asks for it himself. He is the ghostly ancient at the Forlorn Gardens, and the water is to put out his flame.",al={"who is woodwyrd","ancient spirit","rot regret giver"}},{q="Why does the ancient spirit want the flame put out?",a="The spirit says it is burdened by its last mistake and still feels the flame in death.",al={"why put out flame","spirit regret","what was its mistake"}},{q="Where can I find the sacred water?",a="The spirit points you to Maraudon, across Mashan’she, for pristine water from a sacred ravine.",al={"earth song water location","maraudon water","sacred ravine"}},{q="What water does Woodwyrd need?",a="Woodwyrd asks you to bring back a Vial of Earth Song Water.",al={"vial water","what item for woodwyrd","earth song vial"}}},kw={"ancient spirit","earth song water","forlorn gardens","maraudon","mashan’she","rot and regret","sacred ravine","woodwyrd"},rel={"zone:desolace"},m={id=93404},src={"In-game quest text: Rot and Regret"},fv=true}
E["quest:93594"] = {t="quest",n="Word of the Woods",z="shendralas",s="You are asked to find Woodwyrd in the Forlorn Gardens at Shen'dralas. He may know what happened to the gardens and the treants born of the necklace.",h="You are asked to find Woodwyrd in the Forlorn Gardens at Shen'dralas.",sec={{t="A Friend Remembered",b="The gardens’ flowers and trees may hold answers, and you are sent to find Woodwyrd at Shen'dralas in Desolace. He was the greatest of the treants born of the necklace. He cared for every bloom and bud, and sheltered small creatures by rooting himself in the earth at night.",sp=0},{t="The Garden's Keeper",b="Woodwyrd tells you the gardens are lost. He is the last caretaker of his generation, and without the gift, no others can take their place. Weeds cover the land, flowers are restless, and trees wither. He turns toward the ancient whose fire fills the sky.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Woodwyrd?",a="Woodwyrd is a treant born of the necklace and the greatest of his generation. He tended the gardens' blooms and sheltered small creatures at night.",al={"woodwyrd","who's woodwyrd","wood wyrd"}},{q="Where can I find Woodwyrd?",a="You are sent to look for Woodwyrd in the Forlorn Gardens at Shen'dralas in Desolace.",al={"woodwyrd location","find woodwyrd","where is woodwyrd"}},{q="What did Woodwyrd do in the gardens?",a="Woodwyrd tended every bloom and bud. At night, he rooted himself in the ground to shelter small creatures.",al={"woodwyrd job","what did he do","garden caretaker"}},{q="What happened to the treants born of the necklace?",a="The one asking you fears the treants may have fallen and hopes Woodwyrd is still alive to explain what happened.",al={"necklace treants","treants gone","what happened to treants"}},{q="Why is Woodwyrd important?",a="Woodwyrd may know what happened to the treants and the gardens.",al={"why find woodwyrd","woodwyrd matters","why him"}}},kw={"caretaker","desolace","flowers","forlorn gardens","necklace","shen'dralas","treants","woodwyrd"},rel={"zone:shendralas","zone:desolace"},m={id=93594},src={"In-game quest text: Word of the Woods"},fv=true}
E["quest:93601"] = {t="quest",n="Passing the Blame",z="shendralas",s="A witness blames the quilboar for stealing the woman's gift and dooming the garden. You are sent north to the Valley of Bones to seek a quilboar of significance at Bristleback Retreat.",h="A witness blames the quilboar for stealing the woman's gift and dooming the garden.",sec={{t="A Garden in Peril",b="The garden is doomed to die, and the one who saw the theft holds the quilboar responsible. To recover the woman's gift, you are sent north into the Valley of Bones. At Bristleback Retreat, you are to seek out a quilboar of significance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who says the quilboar stole her gift?",a="Not the woman herself. A witness who saw the theft with their own eyebulbs blames the quilboar for taking her gift.",al={"who blames the quilboar","woman's gift","quilboar stole it"}},{q="Where do I go?",a="Head north into the Valley of Bones, to Bristleback Retreat.",al={"where is the valley","where to go","bristleback retreat"}},{q="What am I looking for at Bristleback Retreat?",a="You are to seek out a quilboar of significance at Bristleback Retreat.",al={"who to find","significant quilboar","what's the target"}},{q="Why does the woman blame the quilboar?",a="The blame comes from a witness, not the woman. The witness says the quilboar stole her gift and are why the garden is doomed to die.",al={"why quilboar","why blame them","garden dying"}}},kw={"bristleback retreat","garden","passing the blame","quilboar","valley of bones","woman's gift"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-bones","topic:quilboar"},m={id=93601},src={"In-game quest text: Passing the Blame"},fv=true}
E["quest:93644"] = {t="quest",n="Tattered Journal",z="shendralas",s="A damaged journal found near Shen'dralas points you toward its author, Evenshade. Its missing words may still matter to him.",h="A damaged journal found near Shen'dralas points you toward its author, Evenshade.",sec={{t="A Name Remains",b="Near Shen'dralas, the worn pages of a journal leave you with little to read. Among the blurred letters, one surname stands clear: Evenshade. The author may be somewhere nearby, and the journal's remaining words offer the only lead.",sp=0},{t="The Journal's Fate",b="Mordent recognizes the journal as his, though centuries have passed since he lost it. The writing is gone, but he remembers what it contained and keeps that knowledge to himself. He permits you to try restoring the journal if its pages have survived.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where was the journal found?",a="The journal was found near Shen'dralas.",al={"where journal","tattered journal location"}},{q="Who wrote the journal?",a="The name that remains in the journal points to Evenshade as its author.",al={"journal author","evenshade journal"}},{q="Why look for Evenshade?",a="The journal bears the surname Evenshade, and its author may be somewhere in Shen'dralas.",al={"find evenshade","journal surname"}},{q="Can you read the journal?",a="Most of the journal's knowledge is lost, and the remaining letters are difficult to distinguish.",al={"journal unreadable","what's in journal"}},{q="What does Mordent say about the journal?",a="Mordent identifies it as his lost journal, but says its writing is gone.",al={"mordent journal","who owns journal"}},{q="Will Mordent share what was written?",a="Mordent remembers what the journal contained, but does not wish to speak of it aloud.",al={"journal contents","mordent secret"}}},kw={"damaged journal","evenshade","lost journal","mordent","restore journal","shen'dralas","tattered journal"},rel={"zone:shendralas"},m={id=93644},src={"In-game quest text: Tattered Journal"},fv=true}
E["quest:96010"] = {t="quest",n="Fragments of the Pylons",z="shendralas",s="Mordent Evenshade asks you to recover pylon fragments from the Magram and Gelkis villages in Shen'dralas. The pieces are needed for his work on the damaged pylons.",h="Mordent Evenshade asks you to recover pylon fragments from the Magram and Gelkis villages in Shen'dralas.",sec={{t="Broken Pylons",b="Mordent Evenshade believes centaur rampages damaged both pylons in Shen'dralas. He suspects the Magram and Gelkis carried the scattered shards back to their villages as trophies. You are asked to recover the fragments guarded there and bring them to him.",sp=0},{t="The Crystals",b="Mordent receives the fragments and says the crystals are more broken than he expected. He will keep them for now. Your next step is to gather pliable mana, which can bind the pieces and let leyline power pass through them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks for the pylon fragments?",a="Mordent Evenshade asks you to recover shards and fragments from the Magram and Gelkis villages and return them to him.",al={"who is Mordent","Mordent Evenshade","who wants the crystals"}},{q="Where are the pylon fragments?",a="Mordent believes the Magram and Gelkis took the pylon fragments to their villages in Shen'dralas.",al={"where shards","pylon pieces location","find fragments"}},{q="Why are the pylons damaged?",a="Mordent believes reckless centaur activity damaged both pylons.",al={"what broke pylons","centaur damage","why pylon broken"}},{q="What does Mordent plan to do with the fragments?",a="Mordent plans to bind the broken pieces with pliable mana and use that mana as a conduit for the leylines.",al={"what are crystals for","repair pylons how","mordent plan"}}},kw={"centaur","crystals","fragments of the pylons","gelkis","magram","mana","mordent evenshade","pylon","shards","shen'dralas"},rel={"zone:shendralas","subzone:gelkis-village","topic:centaur"},m={id=96010},src={"In-game quest text: Fragments of the Pylons"},fv=true}
E["quest:96018"] = {t="quest",n="Powering the Pylons",z="shendralas",s="Mordent Evenshade asks you to restore the damaged pylons in Shen'dralas. Floating mana has appeared there, and he needs it gathered and returned to the pylons.",h="Mordent Evenshade asks you to restore the damaged pylons in Shen'dralas.",sec={{t="Gathering Mana",b="Inside Shen'dralas's temple, you seek the Mana Sieve, an artifact its denizens may resent you borrowing. Mordent Evenshade needs the scattered mana gathered in a semicrystallized form. With enough Ancient Mana Crystals, you can empower the damaged pylons and bring the sieve's work back to him.",sp=0},{t="The Pylons",b="Mordent Evenshade sees the pylons restored and gestures toward the sky. He notices your subdued response as he turns back to you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Mordent need mana?",a="Mordent needs mana gathered as Ancient Mana Crystals to empower the damaged pylons in Shen'dralas.",al={"why mana","mordent mana"}},{q="Where do I find the Mana Sieve?",a="The Mana Sieve is inside the temple in Shen'dralas.",al={"mana sieve location","where sieve"}},{q="What is happening to the mana in Shen'dralas?",a="Floating sparks of mana have appeared around Shen'dralas, likely because the pylons have suffered damage.",al={"floating mana","mana orbs"}},{q="What does the Mana Sieve do?",a="You use the Mana Sieve to gather floating mana as Ancient Mana Crystals.",al={"sieve purpose","collect mana"}},{q="Who is asking for the pylons to be empowered?",a="Mordent Evenshade asks you to gather mana and empower the pylons.",al={"who is mordent","mordent evenshade"}}},kw={"ancient mana crystals","floating mana","mana sieve","mordent evenshade","pylons","shen'dralas"},rel={"zone:shendralas"},m={id=96018},src={"In-game quest text: Powering the Pylons"},fv=true}
E["quest:99257"] = {t="quest",n="A Heart of Crystal",z="shendralas",s="Historian Biraxas asks you to recover a Depleted Crystal Heart from a failing pylon protector. The remaining pylon guards may not endure forever.",h="Historian Biraxas asks you to recover a Depleted Crystal Heart from a failing pylon protector.",sec={{t="A Failing Guard",b="Historian Biraxas, within the temple of Shen'dralas, asks you to bring him a Depleted Crystal Heart. The unstable rifts you encountered are precursors to the pylon guards, and Biraxas says his people have been unable to conjure more for centuries. He fears what may happen when the remaining guards fail.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the Crystal Heart?",a="Historian Biraxas asks you to recover a Depleted Crystal Heart and bring it to him within the temple of Shen'dralas.",al={"who wants the heart","Biraxas heart","historian request"}},{q="What is a Depleted Crystal Heart from?",a="It comes from a Decrepit Pylon Protector that is nearly on the verge of collapse.",al={"heart from what","pylon heart","crystal heart source"}},{q="Why does Biraxas want the heart?",a="Biraxas says unstable rifts are precursors to pylon guards, and he worries because no more guards have been conjured for centuries.",al={"why heart needed","what Biraxas wants","pylon protector reason"}},{q="Where do I bring the heart?",a="Bring the Depleted Crystal Heart to Historian Biraxas within the temple of Shen'dralas.",al={"where to take heart","bring it where","Biraxas location"}}},kw={"a heart of crystal","decrepit pylon protector","depleted crystal heart","historian biraxas","pylon guard","shen'dralas","unstable rifts"},rel={"zone:shendralas"},m={id=99257},src={"In-game quest text: A Heart of Crystal"},fv=true}
E["quest:99258"] = {t="quest",n="Mana Mania",z="shendralas",s="Historian Biraxas in the temple of Shen'dralas seeks to learn if enough loose magic remains to conjure protective elementals. By casting a depleted crystal heart into an unstable rift, you can test if the ancient sanctuary still holds the power to craft its own defenses.",h="Historian Biraxas in the temple of Shen'dralas seeks to learn if enough loose magic remains to conjure...",sec={{t="Testing the Rifts",b="Within the temple of Shen'dralas, Historian Biraxas worries that the ancient stronghold lacks the loose mana required to conjure new guardian elementals. Finding the proper gems is difficult enough, yet determining whether any usable magical energy lingers is the true test. Biraxas hands you a depleted crystal heart to cast into an unstable rift. If energy surges forth to animate the stone, the historians will know their sanctuary can still defend itself.",sp=0},{t="A Surge of Energy",b="Hurl the stone into the unstable rift and an elemental stirs, confirming that workable mana still lingers in the sanctuary. Historian Biraxas is stunned by the success after decades of doubt, greeting the breakthrough as an unlife-changing discovery for the Shen'dralas.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Historian Biraxas?",a="Historian Biraxas is a scholar residing in the temple of Shen'dralas who studies methods to restore and maintain defenses for his people.",al={"biraxas","historian biraxas role","who gives mana mania"}},{q="What is the Depleted Crystal Heart?",a="It is a specialized gem vessel designed to absorb ambient magical energy from an unstable mana rift and conjure a defensive elemental.",al={"crystal heart","depleted heart","what is the heart for"}},{q="Why test the unstable mana rifts in Shen'dralas?",a="Historian Biraxas needs to know whether enough loose mana remains in the temple before committing time and research to conjuring guardian elementals.",al={"why test rifts","loose mana shendralas","purpose of rift test"}},{q="What are the Shen'dralas seeking to build?",a="They seek to conjure elementals to serve as defenders for their temple, provided enough ambient magical energy remains.",al={"shendralas elementals","shendralas defenses","why conjuring elementals"}}},kw={"crystal heart","eldre'thalas","elementals","historian biraxas","mana mania","shen'dralas","unstable mana rift"},rel={"zone:shendralas"},m={id=99258},src={"In-game quest text: Mana Mania"},fv=true}
E["subzone:valley-of-bones"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Bones",z="shendralas",s="In Shen'dralas, the Valley of Bones lies choked with dust and ancient remains. Restless dead haunt its canyon, where centaur necromancers patrol among the colossal ribs of two Dead Goliaths.",h="In Shen'dralas, the Valley of Bones lies choked with dust and ancient remains.",sec={{t="A Canyon of the Restless Dead",b="Skeletal horrors walk the dusty ravines of the Valley of Bones, a canyon in the south. Centaur necromancers raise them with dark sorcery and command them. The spirits of the Magram centaur clan wander there too, bound to the barren earth long after their violent deaths. Two immense skeletons, called the Dead Goliaths, slump against the rocky cliffs. Scholars and travelers do not know where they came from.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Dead Goliaths?",a="The Dead Goliaths are the colossal remains of two unknown creatures against the canyon walls. Little is known of their kind or when they died, though their great size suggests beasts from a forgotten era.",al={"giant bones","huge skeletons desolace","dead goliaths lore"}},{q="Why are there centaur ghosts here?",a="The ghosts belong to the Magram, a violent centaur clan native to these arid plains. Unending war between centaur clans and the necromancers' meddling with the dead have denied the Magram spirits rest. They wander the canyon as apparitions.",al={"magram ghosts","why centaur spirits","undead centaur"}},{q="Who controls the skeletons in the valley?",a="Centaur necromancers practice dark rites in the canyon. They raise skeletal servants and command them to guard the crags and hold their ground among the dead.",al={"who commands skeletons","necromancers valley of bones"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you witness the valley's desecration of spirits. Dark practitioners bind Magram souls and raise twisted skeletal servants, perverting death's natural passage."},kw={"centaur","dead goliaths","magram","necromancers","shen'dralas","skeletons","valley of bones"},rel={"zone:shendralas","zone:desolace","topic:centaur"},src={"Valley of Bones"}}
E["zone:shendralas"] = {t="zone",n="Shen'dralas",z="shendralas",s="Centaur, outcasts, and quilboar contest Shen'dralas, south east of desolace. Ancient ruins rise among its crags, between Feralas and Mulgore.",h="Centaur, outcasts, and quilboar contest Shen'dralas, south east of desolace.",sec={{t="A Borderland in Turmoil",b="Shen'dralas lies in the heights south east of desolace, between Mulgore and Feralas. Its craggy passes and hidden enclaves shelter groups struggling to survive far from the great faction capitals. At Evenshade Overlook, some watch from secluded heights. At Outcast Hideaway, others seek refuge where they can be forgotten.",sp=0},{t="Centaur, Quilboar, and Ancient Ruins",b="Ancient ruins recall the highborne legacy behind Shen'dralas's name, yet the land is far from peaceful. Centaur feuds spill across the Magram Front, keeping old bloodshed alive along the borders. Bristleback quilboar hold fortified ground at Bristleback Retreat. Travelers find contested territory in the ravines.",sp=0},{t="The Valley of Bones",b="The valley of bones leads north-west toward Desolace and offers the main overland route into Shen'dralas. Sun and wind have bleached the passage. Its bones recall the violent struggles that still sweep through these crags.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Shen'dralas located?",a="Shen'dralas lies south east of Desolace, between Feralas and Mulgore. Travelers on foot usually enter from Desolace through the Valley of Bones.",al={"where is shendralas","shendralas location","how to get to shendralas"}},{q="Is Shen'dralas controlled by the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Neither the Alliance nor the Horde holds Shen'dralas. Roving centaur, hostile quilboar, outcasts, and isolated encampments make it a contested frontier.",al={"is shendralas horde","is shendralas alliance","who owns shendralas"}},{q="What major settlements or landmarks are here?",a="The main landmarks are the Valley of Bones, Bristleback Retreat, Evenshade Overlook, the Magram Front, Outcast Hideaway, and Shen'dralas's central expanse.",al={"shendralas subzones","landmarks in shendralas","points of interest shendralas"}},{q="Why are there centaur here?",a="Centaur territorial wars reach from Desolace's plains into Shen'dralas along the Magram Front. There, the clan clashes with local defenders and rival factions.",al={"centaur in shendralas","magram front","why are magram here"}},{q="What is Bristleback Retreat?",a="Bristleback Retreat is a fortified outpost held by Bristleback quilboar. They have secured a fierce foothold along the zone's edges.",al={"bristleback retreat","quilboar in shendralas"}},{q="What is the connection between this zone and Lake Dumont?",a="There is no known connection. Shen'dralas has its own landmarks, such as the Valley of Bones and Outcast Hideaway.",al={"lake dumont","shendralas map history"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, Shen'dralas's name recalls the ancient Highborne lore of Eldre'Thalas. Sentinels wary of reckless arcana in southern Kalimdor watch with interest.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, Shen'dralas borders Mulgore and Desolace. Quilboar and centaur aggression along its ridges threatens nearby ancestral hunting grounds.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you cross a remote, contested wilderness with alternate routes between Feralas and central Kalimdor. Travel calls for keen vigilance.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you find Shen'dralas just beyond Mulgore's southern reaches. Keeping the Magram and quilboar contained there helps protect Horde frontiers."},kw={"bristleback retreat","desolace","evenshade overlook","feralas","lake dumont","magram front","mulgore","outcast hideaway","shendralas","Valley of Bones"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-bones","zone:desolace","zone:feralas","zone:mulgore"},src={"Shen'dralas"}}
